opsin/

# Gate run artifacts ( + v22_gate.py completion sentinel)
gate_verdict.json
gate_run.log
# Concurrency locks guarding those artifacts against a second gate. flock-based,
# so they are never stale -- the kernel releases them even on SIGKILL.
*.lock

# JVM crash dumps. 19 of these had accumulated untracked in the repo root and
# were acknowledged in NO doc or commit; they are all from the JPype in-process
# JVM (argv `-Xmx512m -Djava.awt.headless=true --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED`,
# no `-jar`), 15 within three days. Ignoring them keeps `git status` readable --
# it does NOT mean they are benign. The open investigation and what is and is not
# established about their cause:  §H4.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
core.[0-9]*

# v37 SP0 census harness output ():
# a per-molecule JSONL over the full 111,843-unique-SMILES ChEBI corpus is a
# measurement artifact, not source -- keep it local like  output.


# Personal, per-machine  Code overrides. This file was TRACKED until
# 2026-08-04, which put one developer's machine-specific permission allowlist
# (conda paths, absolute /home paths) into the shared repo and would make any
# second developer's local overrides collide with it. `./settings.json`
# stays tracked -- that is the team-wide file, and it carries the agent-teams
# flag plus the guardrails in the contributor guide. Only the `.local.` sibling is personal.
./settings.local.json

